The Single tender route shall be resorted to only in exceptional cases. Single tender may be invited from the registered/ other supplier due to any of the following reasons, duly certified by the Head of the Indenting department (not below the rank of DGM):
a) Proprietary in nature;
b) Purchases from collaborators or from their recommended suppliers;
c) Customer's contract requirement;
d) Urgency of requirement (to be certified by Head of Indenting department/ Product/ Project Manager/ Site-in-charge, with recorded reasons underlying the urgency);
e) Source standardisation;
f) Developmental/Trial orders;
g) Availability of Pattern/ Die/ Special Toolings with a single supplier;
h) Value of purchases being less than Rs. 50,000/- (USD 5,000 for purchases made abroad for foreign site/s);
i) Spares from Original Equipment Manufacturers;
j) Only one registered supplier in the PMD/ SD, subject to fulfilment of the following:
(i) Process at 3.4 is being followed, and
(ii) In case the estimated value of the tender is more than Rs. 20 Lakhs, it shall be recorded that Open tender for procurement has been resorted to in last financial year and there was no new qualified response.
k) Strategic Purchases from CPSEs for items in their manufacturing range, based on sectoral preference guidelines from administrative ministry;
l) Purchases of Non-standard items of R&D projects;
(to be certified by Head of the Indenting department, not below the rank of AGM, that the 'Non-standard' item has been selected in line with BHEL's R&D Policy).
m) Counter Trade arrangements with the approval of the Board;
(to be certified by the concerned Business Sector/ Marketing Group that source/ supplier has been identified as per clause 35.10, and bears the approval of the Competent Authority)
n) Requirements resulting from Strategic tie-ups/ Business Sharing Agreements approved by Functional Director/ CMD.
(to be certified by the concerned Business Group/ Unit that source /supplier/ technology partner has been identified as per clause 35.11, and bears the approval of the Competent Authority)

Re-tendering may be resorted to only after the administrative approval of one step higher than the Competent Authority (limited to Unit Head) for ordering under the circumstances such as:
(a) Inadequate response / Lack of Competition (refer note below);
(b) Unreasonably high/ low price;
(c) Suspected cartel formation;
(d) Sudden slump in market prices;
(e) Major changes in scope and/ or pre-qualification requirement in a tender.
In case L-1 bidder backs out, re-tendering shall be done (without including the L1 bidder who had backed out).
Note:
Inadequate response / Lack of competition shall not be determined solely on the basis of the number of Bidders. Even when only one bid is submitted, the process should be considered valid provided following conditions are satisfied:
(i) The procurement was satisfactorily advertised and sufficient time was given for submission of bids
(ii) The qualification criteria were not unduly restrictive, and
(iii) Prices are reasonable in comparison to market values

Financial concurrence shall necessarily be required for the following:
a) Provision for advance payment, including activity linked payment (drawing/ engg. documentation etc.) in stages;
b) Vetting the comparative statements for ordering proposals requiring Financial Concurrence;
c) Proposal for negotiation/ counteroffer (if any);
d) Proposal for ordering/ FA provided total order value (including amendments) exceeds:
