e) Proposal for amendments to orders having financial implications, except where the order value including amendments is within the limits at (d);
f) Procurement through Empowered Committee;
g) Proposals for Repeat Ordering;
h) Provision for unsecured advance to foreign suppliers;
i) Waiver of Bank Guarantee towards:
- Advance to PSUs/ Government departments.
- Towards safe custody and return of eqUipment after repairs etc.lmaterial after processing/ conversion/ machining etc.
j) Proposals in respect of:
- additional cost implications for which approval was not taken during finalisation of Framework Agreement and
- validity extension of Framework Agreement
k) Escalation claim and/ or provision and approval of PVC in respect of contracts where PVC has not been provided;
I) Sanction of extra items/ substitution of items/ deviation from approved quantities;
m) Reduction/ Waiver of Penalty/ LD;
n) Cancellation of contract;
o) Ex-gratia payment to supplier;
p) Commercial Settlement;
q) Proposals for delivery extensions;
r) Proposals for ordering on Subsidiary/ JV Companies for items within their manufacturing range.

Financial concurrence is not required for the following:
a) Proposals for ordering on sister Units for items within their manufacturing range, including amendmentis;
b) Release of individual purchase/ delivery orders within the approved value of the Framework Agreement;
c) Proposals for Airlifting/ Courier/ Fast Cargo.

It is desirable that the purchase activities relating to the following may be assigned to the respective Functional Heads:
i) Township requirements;
ii) Administrative requirements such as office equipments, stationery and consumables etc;
iii) Medical equipment and hospital/ dispensary requirement (including medicines);
iv) Welfare items, Requirements of Canteen, Guest house and Publicity, Public Relations & CSR related items.
Unit Heads may consider de-centralisation of the above-mentioned purchase activities, keeping in view the Purchase Policy, and may issue necessary instructions in respect of DoP.
